# LARAVEL + VUE + INERTIA STANDARDS

## Laravel
- Use `php artisan make:{type}` to generate all components (controllers, models, migrations, requests, etc.)
- Laravel 11+ removed `app/Console/Kernel.php` — register commands/schedules in `bootstrap/app.php`
- Read environment variables through config files (`config/app.php`, etc.) — never call `env()` outside of a config file
- Avoid N+1 queries — use eager loading (`with()`, `load()`)
- Use soft deletes where the domain calls for recoverable records
- Use Form Requests for validation, not inline validation in controllers

## Vue + Inertia
- Page components live in `resources/js/Pages/`
- Use `<script setup>` (Composition API), not the Options API
- Use `Inertia::render()` server-side for page routing, not a separate API + SPA setup
- Shared/reusable UI goes in `resources/js/Components/`
